     "Hi all,<div>(This is a repost of my post from July 10.  I think I didn&#39;t post properly since I haven&#39;t had any views.  If I did get to the list, I apologize for the redundancy.) </div><div><br></div><div>Before working with real data, I am to recapitulate the causal structure of simulated data.  I have attached a pdf with the causal structure.  Since this is a simulation, I know the true relative strength of various effects. What I am observing is a compression of the estimated variation in effect strength.  Coefficients whose true relative magnitudes are 1:2:3 are being estimated with relative magnitudes of (for example) 1.000000 1.464789 1.842254.  This compression is happening at all points in the model and in repeated simulations.  </div><div><br></div><div>I am not too surprised by this because it is like slope reduction in an error in variables regression.  However, I want to make sure that I am not making some silly mistake, or that there isn&#39;t a bias correction that I am failing to employ.</div><div><br></div><div>lavaan model specification and summary of sem() results below.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks all.</div><div><br></div><div>Best MLT</div><div><br></div><div><div>MAFPC12CC7.sem &lt;- &#39;</div><div>   #Latent variable expression</div><div>   A1 =~ A1.1 + 1*A1.2 + 1*A1.3 + 1*A1.4</div><div>A2 =~ A2.1 + 1*A2.2 + 1*A2.3 + 1*A2.4</div><div>A3 =~ A3.1 + 1*A3.2 + 1*A3.3 + 1*A3.4</div><div>B1 =~ B1.1 + 1*B1.2 + 1*B1.3 + 1*B1.4</div><div>B2 =~ B2.1 + 1*B2.2 + 1*B2.3 + 1*B2.4</div><div>B3 =~ B3.1 + 1*B3.2 + 1*B3.3 + 1*B3.4</div><div>C1 =~ C1.1 + 1*C1.2 + 1*C1.3 + 1*C1.4</div><div>C2 =~ C2.1 + 1*C2.2 + 1*C2.3 + 1*C2.4</div><div>C3 =~ C3.1 + 1*C3.2 + 1*C3.3 + 1*C3.4</div><div>D1 =~ D1.1 + 1*D1.2 + 1*D1.3 + 1*D1.4</div><div>D2 =~ D2.1 + 1*D2.2 + 1*D2.3 + 1*D2.4</div><div>D3 =~ D3.1 + 1*D3.2 + 1*D3.3 + 1*D3.4</div><div>E1 =~ E1.1 + 1*E1.2 + 1*E1.3 + 1*E1.4</div><div>E2 =~ E2.1 + 1*E2.2 + 1*E2.3 + 1*E2.4</div><div>E3 =~ E3.1 + 1*E3.2 + 1*E3.3 + 1*E3.4</div><div>F1 =~ 1*F1.1 + 1*F1.2 + 1*F1.3 + 1*F1.4</div><div>F2 =~ 1*F2.1 + 1*F2.2 + 1*F2.3 + 1*F2.4</div><div>F3 =~ 1*F3.1 + 1*F3.2 + 1*F3.3 + 1*F3.4</div><div>A1+A2+A3 =~ FA</div><div>B1+B2+B3 =~ FB</div><div>C1+C2+C3 =~ FC</div><div>D1+D2+D3 =~ FD</div><div>E1+E2+E3 =~ FE</div><div>F1+F2+F3 =~ FF</div><div>FA+FB+FC=~PC1</div><div>FD+FE+FF =~ PC2</div><div>PC1+PC2 =~ CC</div><div>CC =~ obCC</div><div># residual variances</div><div>A1.1~~v1*A1.1</div></div><div>#bunch of lines like the above to enforce equality of variances </div><div>&#39;</div><div><br></div><div><div>&gt; summary(MAFPC12CC7.fit,standardized=T)</div><div>lavaan (0.5-13) converged normally after 119 iterations</div><div><br></div><div>  Number of observations                         10000</div><div><br></div><div>  Estimator                                         ML</div><div>  Minimum Function Test Statistic             3064.355</div><div>  Degrees of freedom                              2524</div><div>  P-value (Chi-square)                           0.000</div><div><br></div><div>Parameter estimates:</div><div><br></div><div>  Information                                 Expected</div><div>  Standard Errors                             Standard</div><div><br></div><div>                   Estimate  Std.err  Z-value  P(&gt;|z|)   Std.lv  Std.all</div><div>Latent variables:</div><div>  A1 =~</div><div>    A1.1              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>    A1.2              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>    A1.3              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>    A1.4              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>  A2 =~</div><div>    A2.1              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>    A2.2              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>    A2.3              1.000                               0.452    0.861</div><div>