    [
     3,
     "<div><div><br>On Friday, July 12, 2013 3:21:41 AM UTC-6, Yves Rosseel wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">This looks odd:\r\n<br>\r\n<br>&gt; A1+A2+A3 =~ FA\r\n<br>&gt; B1+B2+B3 =~ FB\r\n<br>&gt; C1+C2+C3 =~ FC\r\n<br>&gt; D1+D2+D3 =~ FD\r\n<br>&gt; E1+E2+E3 =~ FE\r\n<br>&gt; F1+F2+F3 =~ FF\r\n<br>&gt; FA+FB+FC=~PC1\r\n<br>&gt; FD+FE+FF =~ PC2\r\n<br>&gt; PC1+PC2 =~ CC\r\n<br>&gt; CC =~ obCC\r\n<br>\r\n<br>According to your path diagram, A-F is regressed on the a1-f3 factors; \r\n<br>they are not &#39;second&#39; order factors. So your syntax should be:\r\n<br>\r\n<br>FA ~ A1 + A2 + A3\r\n<br>FB ~ B1 + B2 + B3\r\n<br>...\r\n<br>PC1 ~ FA + FB + FC\r\n<br>PC2 ~ FD + FE + FF\r\n<br>CC ~ PC1 + PC2\r\n<br>obCC ~ CC\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Yves.\r\n<br>\r\n<br></blockquote></div></div>"
